chapter BRIDGITTE_FIRST_MEETING:
    narrator "The small house smells faintly of woodsmoke, dried herbs, and oiled leather."
    narrator "A woman stands near the table, cleaning an old dagger with a practiced hand."
    narrator "She looks up when you enter. Her eyes are calm, but guarded."

    bridgitte "You're standing straighter than yesterday."
    bridgitte "That's good."
    bridgitte "Means the poultices worked, or you're too stubborn to admit they didn't."

    player "You were one of the people who found me?"

    bridgitte "One of them, yes."
    bridgitte "You were half-buried in mud, bruised purple, and breathing like each breath had to be argued into you."
    bridgitte "Not the sort of thing a decent person walks past."

    player "I don't remember how I got here."

    bridgitte "Figured as much."
    bridgitte "People who know where they are don't usually wake up asking which country they're in."

    player "The chief told me this is Kingdom Alpha."

    bridgitte "Western edge of it."
    bridgitte "Arkama province. Closest real city is Arkama, and even that feels far when the roads are bad."
    bridgitte "Past the village, there's mountain, forest, and then ocean."
    bridgitte "Not much farther west to go unless you plan on learning to breathe saltwater."

    player "I need to go back to Beta."

    bridgitte "The Duchy of Beta?"
    bridgitte "That's not impossible."
    bridgitte "But it's not a walk down the lane either. A month by carriage if the roads are kind, the tolls are paid, and nothing with teeth decides your horse looks edible."

    player "Then I should leave as soon as I can."

    bridgitte "No."
    bridgitte "You should live long enough to leave."

    player "What do you mean?"

    bridgitte "I mean this village is quiet, not safe."
    bridgitte "We've got game, livestock, clean wells, good soil. That draws people."
    bridgitte "It also draws predators."
    bridgitte "Wolves when winter runs lean. Boars when the mast is poor. Coyotes from the Arkama brush when their packs get bold."
    bridgitte "And monsters, now and then."

    player "I don't know how to fight."

    bridgitte "I know."

    player "Is it that obvious?"

    bridgitte "To me, yes."
    bridgitte "You hold yourself like someone who's never had to watch another person's shoulders."
    bridgitte "And when the village chief dropped that pan behind you this morning, you froze instead of moving."
    bridgitte "No shame in it."
    bridgitte "But shame won't keep blood inside your body."

    player "So you want to teach me?"

    bridgitte "If you're willing to learn."

    player "Why help me that much?"

    bridgitte "Because we helped you once already."
    bridgitte "And because kindness ought to move in circles, not stop at one person."
    bridgitte "You want your strength back? Good. I can help with that."
    bridgitte "In return, you help me with the culling work around the village."

    player "Culling work?"

    bridgitte "Predators that get too close. Burrows that spread too fast. Little things, mostly."
    bridgitte "The sort of work a quest board would handle if this place had one."
    bridgitte "It doesn't."
    bridgitte "So it comes to me."

    player "Are you an adventurer?"

    bridgitte "Was."

    player "You stopped?"

    bridgitte "I stopped."
    bridgitte "Now I hunt, mend fences, track prints, pull children out of places they were told not to climb, and keep monsters away from goats that seem determined to die creatively."

    player "That sounds like an official job."

    bridgitte "It isn't."
    bridgitte "Official jobs come with official pay."
    bridgitte "I get eggs, smoked meat, apologies, and the occasional loaf of bread left on my step by someone pretending they didn't leave it."

    narrator "She sets the cleaned dagger on the table."

    bridgitte "This was mine, years ago."
    bridgitte "Not my best blade. Not my prettiest."
    bridgitte "But it kept me alive when I knew less than I thought I did."

    player "You're giving it to me?"

    bridgitte "Lending."
    bridgitte "If you die with it, I'll be cross."

    player "I'll try not to."

    bridgitte "Good."
    bridgitte "Try harder than that."

    narrator "Bridgitte picks the dagger up by the flat of the blade and offers you the handle."

    bridgitte "Short blade arts."
    bridgitte "Knives and daggers. Close work. Quick work."
    bridgitte "Not heroic, not pretty, and not something bards sing about unless the bard owes somebody money."
    bridgitte "But for someone starting from nothing, it teaches the right lessons."
    bridgitte "Distance. Timing. Hands. Feet. When to move, when not to."

    player "I don't feel ready."

    bridgitte "You're not."
    bridgitte "That's why we start with something that won't eat you if you make one mistake."

    player "What do you need me to do?"

    bridgitte "There's an Arkama coyote skulking near the lower path."
    bridgitte "Thin thing. Mean. Probably pushed out of its pack."
    bridgitte "It has been testing the chicken fences and following children at dusk."

    player "You want me to kill it?"

    bridgitte "I want you to learn why holding a blade is different from using one."
    bridgitte "I'll show you the basics first."
    bridgitte "After that, you go to the forest edge and deal with the coyote."
    bridgitte "I'll be nearby."

    player "Nearby enough to help?"

    bridgitte "Nearby enough that you learn."
    bridgitte "Not so near that you lean on me."

    choice:
        -> "I'll do it. Teach me.":
            player "I'll do it."
            player "Teach me."

            bridgitte "Good."
            bridgitte "First lesson."
            bridgitte "A dagger is not a sword that lost ambition."
            bridgitte "Keep it close. Keep your wrist alive. Never show the point unless you mean to use it."
            bridgitte "And if you ever think a fight is fair, assume you missed something."

            narrator "Bridgitte steps outside and gestures for you to follow."
            narrator "The village air is cool. Somewhere nearby, livestock shift and mutter behind their fences."
            narrator "Your hand closes around the old dagger."

            call unlockCombatClass("ruffian")
            call giveItem("old_dagger")
            call startQuest("cull_arkama_coyote")
            call unlockLocation("forest_edge")
            call unlockActivity("coyote_culling")

            set bridgitte_intro_done = true
            set bridgitte_lore_unlocked = true
            set quest_cull_coyote_started = true

            bridgitte "Come on, then."
            bridgitte "Before that coyote grows bold enough to think this village belongs to it."

        -> "I don't have much choice, do I?":
            player "I don't have much choice, do I?"

            bridgitte "You always have a choice."
            bridgitte "Some choices are just worse than others."

            player "That's not very reassuring."

            bridgitte "It wasn't meant to be."
            bridgitte "Reassurance is for after you've survived the lesson."

            bridgitte "First lesson."
            bridgitte "A dagger is not a sword that lost ambition."
            bridgitte "Keep it close. Keep your wrist alive. Never show the point unless you mean to use it."
            bridgitte "And if you ever think a fight is fair, assume you missed something."

            call unlockCombatClass("ruffian")
            call giveItem("old_dagger")
            call startQuest("cull_arkama_coyote")
            call unlockLocation("forest_edge")
            call unlockActivity("coyote_culling")

            set bridgitte_intro_done = true
            set bridgitte_lore_unlocked = true
            set quest_cull_coyote_started = true

            bridgitte "Come on."
            bridgitte "We'll put some sense into your feet before we put you in front of teeth."

        -> "What if I can't do it?":
            player "What if I can't do it?"

            bridgitte "Then you step back."
            bridgitte "You breathe."
            bridgitte "You try again."
            bridgitte "And if trying again would get you killed, you run."

            player "That doesn't sound very heroic."

            bridgitte "Good."
            bridgitte "Heroes die because they think running is beneath them."
            bridgitte "Survivors get to decide what kind of person they become after."

            bridgitte "First lesson."
            bridgitte "A dagger is not a sword that lost ambition."
            bridgitte "Keep it close. Keep your wrist alive. Never show the point unless you mean to use it."
            bridgitte "And if you ever think a fight is fair, assume you missed something."

            call unlockCombatClass("ruffian")
            call giveItem("old_dagger")
            call startQuest("cull_arkama_coyote")
            call unlockLocation("forest_edge")
            call unlockActivity("coyote_culling")

            set bridgitte_intro_done = true
            set bridgitte_lore_unlocked = true
            set quest_cull_coyote_started = true

            bridgitte "Come on."
            bridgitte "We'll start slow. Slow is better than dead."
